From cb3f376bc2338f09c9a81e552d3a8789e849bd80 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 10:59:49 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 43/43] GE: environment (shade) mapping, texture map mode 2

Texture map mode 2 (0xC0 bits 0-1) was ignored and drawn with the vertex
UVs. The vertex shader now makes U and V as (1 + N.L) / 2 from the
world-space normal and the vectors of the two lights 0xC1 names (bits 0-1
and 8-9), whatever their types and enables, scaled by the texture scale
and not offset. A light vector never set is taken as (0, 0, 1), and so is
a vertex without a normal, in world space, as the lighting takes it. The
light indices and reverse normals ride in the object block (texgen), which
env-mapped draws now write and record for frame interpolation as lit draws
do.

<prefix>_NO_ENV_MAP uses the vertex UVs, as before; <prefix>_ENV_MAP_OFFSET
adds the texture offset; <prefix>_TRACE_ENV_MAP[=N] logs the first draws.
The census counts texmap.env_map_drawn (info) unless NO_ENV_MAP.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
